# Line endings are pinned to LF in the WORKING TREE, not just in the index.
#
# Why this matters here specifically (I-020): core.autocrlf is true on at least
# one of the two machines this repository is cloned on (I-018). Without this
# file, `git pull` checks the committed CSVs out as CRLF, while re-running
# data-raw/generate_synthetic_data.R writes them as LF. The checksums then
# differ for a reason that has nothing to do with the seed — and "a seeded
# script reproduces this data exactly" is a claim made on screen during the
# demonstration (D-001).
#
# LF also matches Connect Cloud's Linux build host, so the deployed bytes are
# the bytes that were tested locally.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Committed Quarto render output — leave untouched.
*.png binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
